# Line endings decide package bytes, and package bytes are this repository's
# release evidence. Without these rules a clone's core.autocrlf setting changes
# the ZIP checksum without any source change, so recorded hashes in #1, #19 and
# #20 could not be reproduced on another machine.
#
# Everything checks out with the endings named here rather than the local
# setting, so the working tree, the flat package and the installed runtime are
# byte-identical on every machine.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows PowerShell owns setup and validation; keep its historical CRLF bytes.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# The pre-push secret scan runs under sh and must stay LF.
.githooks/pre-push text eol=lf

# Reviewed runtime assets: never transform.
*.jpg -text
*.gif -text
